#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228895 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "38be687e-4fea-5e8a-a810-4c7f50667ea8" :question/math-academy-id "e-21842" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/e70e54b6a70cebd480b86baf9d0e1d90bde0b3d9277c982d5d5e77218d0d2f5d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/48965cee8a09df4f637b4d997fdb9c90673e69a90ea1320434f9b471a2fed280.png)\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{2t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{(2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s \\leq 0.$\n\nFor $s > 0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{(2-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-s}{[{e}^{(2-s)t}]}_{0}^{3}+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3(2-s)}-1}{2-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s > 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228904 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "f8786fd7-c9d5-5ada-9aa0-faa2a45f4cd9" :question/math-academy-id "e-6641" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s) = \\mathcal L\\{f(t)\\}$ for $f(t) = u(t - 2) + u(t-6),$ where $u$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-6),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-2) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 2\\end{aligned} \\\\ u(t-6) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<6 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043349/assets/6ddb2983dec1f3221778a336bb6ef3cce3138476b67d64334ab6660184a79f95.png)\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{6}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for $s \\leq 0.$\n\nFor $s > 0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{6}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{6}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{2}^{6}+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{6}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-6s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}(0-{e}^{-6s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-6s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-6s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}\\left\\{f(t)\\right\\} =\\dfrac{e^{-2s}}{s} +\\dfrac{e^{-6s}}{s}, \n\\qquad \ns > 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e21e27ad-34cb-551e-beb0-9fdef7a86088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-5s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373868} {:answer/id #uuid "cf36838c-ff48-5e53-80de-138e02058a38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}({e}^{-5s}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373869} {:answer/id #uuid "717b84c8-0e96-58bf-84bc-1948b3da34ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373870} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3ba88f-acfe-516c-814e-29681aa1eba4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-5s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "717b84c8-0e96-58bf-84bc-1948b3da34ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373870} :answer-field/id #uuid "74f47699-2694-5266-a56e-bc96d91cf802" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a4cacbc-5afe-5933-a4d7-e3e3664819fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-340886" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $s>0,$ where $f(t)=u(5-t)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(5-t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(5-t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute this integral for $s>0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-5s})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2218c82-e0fe-506a-a589-71fd63a74ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373874} {:answer/id #uuid "ad54bee2-24a0-5962-9c66-5cf55e33a6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373875} {:answer/id #uuid "2857b654-b96c-5693-bdde-fe51c492cc3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373876} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3d9dfb-2596-50b1-8754-972c61b166cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373877} {:answer/id #uuid "42dde035-4931-5008-8d90-8ba652f1a12f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}+\\frac{2}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2857b654-b96c-5693-bdde-fe51c492cc3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373876} :answer-field/id #uuid "846094c0-121d-5b5c-9cf0-12a30fd17c38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb03899-44d9-5e3c-ac1a-400c9922ea58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373880} {:answer/id #uuid "995ec693-0406-5bf9-ba50-674d81c0c350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373881} {:answer/id #uuid "ec0a59ff-3035-5682-b1dd-c1c0f033e955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373882} {:answer/id #uuid "f50a1035-d7e5-594b-83d8-f78405e40a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f50a1035-d7e5-594b-83d8-f78405e40a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373883} :answer-field/id #uuid "7582edcb-4623-5a6e-9189-b5330e7ed5a3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25e532b1-d332-5b0d-bf0b-74f3f071e83b" :question/math-academy-id "q-340932" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\, & x\\le 4 \\\\ 1\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa4e5ea-4212-52bb-9bc8-fffb0353923e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-3s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fa4e5ea-4212-52bb-9bc8-fffb0353923e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{-3s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373886} :answer-field/id #uuid "46b2494e-1156-5ff2-9b36-95e598c10e6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1170717d-397e-54bd-9e39-81a6a2934376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1170717d-397e-54bd-9e39-81a6a2934376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373888} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1333bc-25d9-54dc-8549-d527d0bf7b38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1758e97-d042-5ad6-8009-2fa1ad1a4ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1758e97-d042-5ad6-8009-2fa1ad1a4ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373890} :answer-field/id #uuid "872136bb-f2c4-5e8f-a398-dc46f743887c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0249688-b769-5c6c-909c-995e30a9535e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341390" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)=u(t-3)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.\n\n$F(s)=L{f(t)}=$\n{{field-1}},\nvalid for $s\\,$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-3)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<3 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(t-3){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate this integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{s}(0-{e}^{-3s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s},\\,s>0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dc4e037-c2ef-5b6f-8344-e7aac2fb8795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373893} {:answer/id #uuid "b38573a6-44db-565c-aff6-a067b0c22c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}({e}^{-8s}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373894} {:answer/id #uuid "589c5a75-15cb-5712-b9b1-06accaa7d458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-8s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373895} {:answer/id #uuid "cafef4e6-f7c8-50cb-87df-c122286c0964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s}(1+{e}^{-8s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dc4e037-c2ef-5b6f-8344-e7aac2fb8795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373893} :answer-field/id #uuid "218750eb-e2c4-5ce3-befb-f9a63487f08d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "794abdcb-950e-54b9-b040-f1e3c0111c67" :question/math-academy-id "q-341398" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $s>0,$ where $f(t)=u(8-t)$ and $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(8-t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & t\\le 8 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>8\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }u(8-t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe compute this integral for $s>0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{8}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{0}^{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-8s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{-8s})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49df0af0-4866-5f7f-ba09-cb3533fcdf4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373899} {:answer/id #uuid "9109ca01-a456-5192-b2d7-1c197cad2526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373900} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd01628-e192-5fc7-883d-90b88b555f70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373901} {:answer/id #uuid "59ca0f94-da97-5142-9fcd-bb4f1ea97c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(s-3)}}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9109ca01-a456-5192-b2d7-1c197cad2526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373900} :answer-field/id #uuid "d273da79-24fa-5734-b229-e74047459f49" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373898} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0cf8da6-0839-5072-89fc-b6dc3b80316f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373904} {:answer/id #uuid "557cf367-1d23-581b-b5d3-413eeab5991b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373905} {:answer/id #uuid "35545415-42b6-58d1-a397-637351e7e888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373906} {:answer/id #uuid "47a1d770-c97d-54f2-9031-a81ae344cf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373907} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0d76ba-5e5d-506f-a808-7d78b40b0a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373908} {:answer/id #uuid "bf90cf3e-f4bf-54aa-b7d0-23583cf481c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cf8da6-0839-5072-89fc-b6dc3b80316f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373904} :answer-field/id #uuid "b83761ba-1261-5c52-8df2-4e5b9426529f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83e320ec-a2b6-5adc-99bf-a554f2f85706" :question/math-academy-id "q-341451" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\, & t>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & t\\le 5 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\, & t>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 3.$\n\nFor $s>3,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}3{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{5}+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{5}^{a}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{e}^{(3-s)t}}{3-s})|}_{5}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{3-s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{(3-s)a}-{e}^{5(3-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{3-s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{5(3-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{s}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{5(3-s)}}{s-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd2d0c0-bb5c-50fe-98ca-b9dfaaf8b330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{s-3}-\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373912} {:answer/id #uuid "84404090-eda9-5908-8e16-9b5bad402cb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}}{s-3}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373913} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc232e8-2dc8-53f6-b0dc-690aa618c040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2(s-3)}}{s-3}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373914} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5d6648-1128-5004-a8d4-450f0972e74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c5d6648-1128-5004-a8d4-450f0972e74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373915} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2889bc9-5d6b-53ee-9193-c9cc4ae00d1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8c2a0a6-42a8-5af2-948e-a56bd944ca36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373917} {:answer/id #uuid "58f4c4bc-02d0-5fc0-b9fd-aeb956b430fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373918} {:answer/id #uuid "638800b1-aefe-5619-bee1-b19e8b1841c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373919} {:answer/id #uuid "c7db5802-9e69-51ae-9d6a-0dbecf5ac0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373920} {:answer/id #uuid "60764d08-610f-5531-841e-fa7037f3fc98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373921} {:answer/id #uuid "e1184993-4dfa-5eba-87a5-994ebc8d9e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1184993-4dfa-5eba-87a5-994ebc8d9e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373922} :answer-field/id #uuid "b09dc0a7-00c9-549a-9bcd-3830d1ce9e71" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5b3901e-c1c6-5348-864d-60f3574ecd1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-341464" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t},\\, & t\\le 2 \\\\ 2\\, & t>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{(3-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-s}{[{e}^{(3-s)t}]}_{0}^{2}+{\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-2{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-2s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3-s)}-1}{3-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af9302d-4367-54c0-b22a-9deecb964a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373925} {:answer/id #uuid "ca32bd51-ae12-5a44-8d62-f918865cf7f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{s-5}-\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373926} {:answer/id #uuid "55001533-e234-53a1-80b2-d941ca1d2c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(s-5)}}{s-5}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373927} {:answer/id #uuid "245cb87e-801d-5b1d-a94e-46ff67fb547f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}}{s-5}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1af9302d-4367-54c0-b22a-9deecb964a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373925} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae080da8-6158-5e1e-8007-2055e042dcd1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373924} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f74b45a3-64b0-5dd8-b50f-a611882d3ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373930} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ae94e4-29ba-599a-b2dc-d0533db01296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373931} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fad298-2b55-57f1-adbc-517c91c39c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373932} {:answer/id #uuid "59a16b0c-1ac0-5fcc-b56f-df90f8d79909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373933} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf0b984-0295-5875-b875-fa087ea490ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373934} {:answer/id #uuid "cba23107-83bc-5ed0-9a4a-0d0d97bd7d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cba23107-83bc-5ed0-9a4a-0d0d97bd7d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373935} :answer-field/id #uuid "98b28611-7ed9-537e-a6d8-23bb4fbe9332" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cf6501c-88d1-5bcb-ba50-40bbf2b67514" :question/math-academy-id "q-341465" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 1\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{5t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{(5-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5-s}{[{e}^{(5-s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}-\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{(5-s)}-1}{5-s}+\\frac{{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "470eba5b-2b04-5798-9b88-6dafaa927aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4(s-1)}}{s-1}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373938} {:answer/id #uuid "336b128c-7996-512e-b124-c18e9364d65c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373939} {:answer/id #uuid "fa01c01b-ea70-5ed7-bf48-8b8d2386c492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}}{s-1}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373940} {:answer/id #uuid "470b7550-067e-5a9a-8211-5290fa6bd6ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{s-1}-\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "336b128c-7996-512e-b124-c18e9364d65c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373939} :answer-field/id #uuid "67217846-8af4-5f74-bc86-d2a95b2cf262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe10f32-6bd2-51f4-9181-8a35117f5dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373943} {:answer/id #uuid "48f1c7f7-05f6-547b-b846-ede14161c2b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373944} {:answer/id #uuid "ceabe3b2-b149-5d4d-b23f-037e6227a268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373945} {:answer/id #uuid "7b1129ff-af75-58d5-ab16-a7e136fbd038" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373946} {:answer/id #uuid "aa12e72c-64f8-5a61-915c-648b5fe9222e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373947} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c891c-d214-52b6-9067-cc0dfaa105ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f8c891c-d214-52b6-9067-cc0dfaa105ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373948} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5d7212-5b3c-5ba4-8232-f73f72534e2b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e29c720d-2e98-5ba0-939c-6a32ce63eeb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341466" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t},\\, & t\\le 4 \\\\ 2\\, & t>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t},\\, & t\\le 4 \\\\ 2\\, & t>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-s}{[{e}^{(1-s)t}]}_{0}^{4}+{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{4}^{a}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-2{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{4}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-4s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4(1-s)}-1}{1-s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-4s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29141fda-93f4-5320-b937-46ef6d25bbdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-(3+s)}-1}{s+3}-\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373951} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1d200d-2e09-5362-884c-7a4c528b8b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-(3+s)}}{s+3}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373952} {:answer/id #uuid "3346567b-1a26-5214-812b-53d765768bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373953} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9850bf-160a-528a-b7c1-2ab99eae6ce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{(3+s)}}{s+3}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3346567b-1a26-5214-812b-53d765768bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373953} :answer-field/id #uuid "196bb3ae-ca9f-5fe1-8813-5a3d4db085e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044af014-4734-5c55-8e47-caaec0f9c498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373956} {:answer/id #uuid "f9450133-089b-5237-b8d2-5b0f6c1833be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373957} {:answer/id #uuid "ea02b155-e202-550b-996b-370952eabe36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373958} {:answer/id #uuid "016a2796-8cfc-5c14-8333-c840d955f174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373959} {:answer/id #uuid "d58d4808-2379-5442-9651-792872929ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373960} {:answer/id #uuid "66a1a33d-20d9-5244-96e0-77e092475b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d58d4808-2379-5442-9651-792872929ab6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373960} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eb756d5-9c0e-5bf5-9b3f-ad6f77920e72" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "472a84d4-71fc-53d1-84b9-c9c734ba9c9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341481" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t},\\, & t\\le 1 \\\\ 4\\, & t>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-3t-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{-(3+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-(3+s)}{[{e}^{-(3+s)t}]}_{0}^{1}+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}4{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{-4{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-as}-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}-\\frac{4}{s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{-s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-(3+s)}}{3+s}+\\frac{4{e}^{-s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8d56e41-d8d3-5a99-b322-e2fa2106ade0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}={e}^{-7s}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373964} {:answer/id #uuid "760fb3c7-cbde-50dd-9475-960194142730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}(1-{e}^{7s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373965} {:answer/id #uuid "d44c7d37-1812-5c96-a915-a6fc7aa5d7bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}=\\frac{1}{7}({e}^{3s}-{e}^{s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373966} {:answer/id #uuid "7213617b-94ad-58e2-a114-21381474718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373967} {:answer/id #uuid "8658aed8-844d-5bdc-8f89-c8c630879826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}={e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7213617b-94ad-58e2-a114-21381474718f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "L{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373967} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0d5ec79-f08f-57a3-a902-728d652ef71a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00dd8ce2-12a0-578b-bdb4-79fe7d1127f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-89515" :question/problem "Find $L{f(t)}$ for the piecewise function defined by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<1 \\\\ -7,\\, & 1\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the piecewise function \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)={\\begin{aligned}0\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,t<1 \\\\ -7\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,1\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{for}\\,\\,t>3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}(-7){e}^{-st}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate this definite integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(-7){e}^{-st}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{7}{s}{e}^{-st}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{7}{s}({e}^{-3s}-{e}^{-s}).\n$$"}]}
